SUMMARY:Tech Internships Panel
LOCATION:Computer Science Building 105
DESCRIPTION:A panel of current students who have interned for tech compan
 ies will talk about their experiences and provide an inside look at what
  it's like to work in software engineering\, machine learning\, quant\, 
 product management and research. You'll learn how to navigate the applic
 ation process\, prepare for interviews\, and stand out to employers. Whe
 ther you just started exploring opportunities or are actively pursuing i
 nternships\, this discussion will offer practical advice and firsthand p
 erspectives to help you take the next step. This program is co-sponsored
  by the COS Council and the Center for Career Development\, and it is op
 en to all Princeton University undergraduate and graduate students regar
 dless of identity. Email [careerdevelopment@princeton.edu](mailto:career
 development@princeton.edu) to request accommodations at least two weeks 
 prior to the program.\nAudience: Graduate Students\, Undergraduate Stude
 nts\nRegister: https://princeton.joinhandshake.com/edu/events/2028722\nh
 ttps://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/tech-internships-panel
URL:https://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/tech-internships-panel
